        <mxCell id="uZkxOawaXXojzZYL6WzT-94" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(28, 43, 51); font-family: Optimistic, system-ui, -apple-system, &amp;quot;system-ui&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;.SFNSText-Regular&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: start; white-space-collapse: preserve-breaks; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;When training with batch sizes greater than 1 (BS &amp;gt; 1), we need to preload all audio files and concatenate them into a single, long audio sequence. This is necessary because batching audio files of varying lengths is non-trivial. Additionally, we must keep track of each individual audio file&#39;s length to facilitate the generation of audio encodings (tokens) for each file during the encoding stage, where the concatenated audio will be split back into individual files.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="10" y="450" width="180" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
